Here is the modified sequence of client requests with the addition of the STOR and HELP commands in ap requests, we can insert them at appropziate locations. Here’s a modified sequence that includes both commands:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
NOOP            ; This command can be added after establishing the connection and before listing
LIST
RMD mydirectory ; This command can be added after listing,the contents, assuming you want to remove a directory named "mydirectory"uence that includes is modifned sequence:

- The NOOP command is added after the PORT command to ensure that the connection is alive.
- The RMD command is added after the LIST command, assuming you want to remove a directory after listing the contents of the current directory.

Please replace "mydirectory" with the actual name of the directory you wish to remove


```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
HELP
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
LIST
STOR filename.txt
QUIT
```

